---
import BackToTop from '../components/BackToTop.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy" description="Privacy policy for the Reaktor app and website.">
  <SiteHeader />

  <div class="page-shell">
    <main class="container privacy-page" data-pagefind-body>
      <section class="section legal-panel" data-reveal>
        <h1 class="page-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Reaktor collects nothing of its own. Your games stay on your device; the Android app's
          ads come from Google AdMob. Effective October 2, 2026.
        </p>

        <div class="privacy-strip" aria-label="Privacy summary">
          <span><strong>No accounts</strong></span>
          <span><strong>Games stay on your device</strong></span>
          <span><strong>Ads from Google AdMob, Android only</strong></span>
          <span><strong>Your consent where the law requires it</strong></span>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-copy section-tight">
          <article class="policy-row">
              <h2>Who we are</h2>
              <p>
                Reaktor is a local multiplayer strategy game for Android, developed by Shravan
                Goswami, Jitendra Verma and Ayaan Shaikh, and published on Google Play by Shravan
                Goswami. This policy covers the Reaktor app on Google Play, the web version, and
                this website.
              </p>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-row">
              <h2>What the app collects</h2>
              <p>
                Nothing of its own. Reaktor has no accounts, no analytics and no crash reporting of
                its own, and the game sends nothing to us. The only data that leaves the Android app
                is what Google's ads and Google Play collect, described below. We do not receive
                that data ourselves: AdMob shows us only totals, such as how many ads were shown.
              </p>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-row">
              <h2>Data stored on your device</h2>
              <p>
                Game sessions, board settings, sound and haptic preferences, and the local
                leaderboard (including any player names you type during setup) are saved only in the
                app's private storage on your device. They never leave it. You can erase everything
                at any time from Settings (Clear All Game History, Clear Leaderboard) or by
                uninstalling the app.
              </p>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-row">
              <h2>Ads in the Android app</h2>
              <p>
                The Android app shows ads through Google AdMob, using the Google Mobile Ads SDK.
                They are kept away from play: a small banner at the bottom of the game list,
                leaderboard, rules, settings and about screens, and now and then a full-screen ad
                as you leave a finished match, never after your first match and never during one.
                Ads are limited to content rated PG, suitable for most audiences with parental
                guidance.
              </p>
              <p>
                To show ads, measure how they perform and prevent fraud, the SDK collects your
                device's advertising ID and other device identifiers, your approximate location
                worked out from your IP address, how you interact with ads, and diagnostics such as
                how the app and the ads perform, and sends it to Google. Google uses this data
                under
                <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
                  how Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services</a>
                and
                <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
                  Google's privacy policy</a>. Without a connection no ads are requested and nothing
                is sent, and the game plays as usual.
              </p>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-row">
              <h2>Your choices about ads</h2>
              <p>
                When the app starts, it checks with Google's consent tool, the User Messaging
                Platform, before it asks for any ads. Where the law requires a choice, such as in
                the European Economic Area, the UK and Switzerland, and in some US states, it shows
                Google's consent form first, and Privacy Choices in Settings opens it again so you
                can change your answer. Ads that are not personalised still use some data, for
                example to limit how often you see the same ad, to measure it and to prevent fraud.
                You can reset or delete your advertising ID, or turn off personalised ads, in your
                phone's settings, under Privacy and then Ads, or Google and then Ads.
              </p>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-row">
              <h2>The Supporter pack</h2>
              <p>
                The Android app offers one optional purchase, the Supporter pack, which turns its
                ads off for good. Google Play Billing handles the purchase from start to finish:
                your payment details go to Google, under Google's privacy policy and
                <a href="https://play.google.com/about/play-terms/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
                  Google Play's terms</a>, and never reach us. The app learns only whether the pack
                was bought: it asks Google Play when it starts, and remembers the answer on your
                device.
              </p>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-row">
              <h2>The web version</h2>
              <p>
                When you play Reaktor in a browser, it shows no ads, sells nothing, and loads no ad
                or billing code. Your games and settings are saved in your browser's storage for
                this site and are never sent to us.
              </p>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-row">
              <h2>Permissions</h2>
              <p>
                The Android app has network access, which the ads and the Supporter pack need:
                Google's ads SDK adds the internet, network state and advertising ID permissions,
                the permissions Android's own ad privacy features use, and the wake lock and
                foreground service permissions its background tasks need, and Google Play Billing
                adds its billing permission. It asks for no location,
                camera, microphone, contacts or files. Links in the app (such as developer pages or
                the Play Store listing) open in your browser or the Play app, where those services'
                own policies apply.
              </p>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-row">
              <h2>Children</h2>
              <p>
                Reaktor is a strategy game anyone can enjoy, but it is not directed at children
                under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them. The ads
                in the Android app are limited to content rated PG. If you believe a child under 13
                has used the app and have a question about their data, email us.
              </p>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-row">
              <h2>Google Play</h2>
              <p>
                The app is distributed through Google Play. Google may process platform-level data
                (such as install statistics or crash telemetry) as described in
                <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
                  Google's privacy policy</a>. That processing happens outside the app.
              </p>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-row">
              <h2>This website</h2>
              <p>
                The site is a static site hosted on GitHub Pages; GitHub may log standard request
                data as described in
                <a
                  href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noreferrer"
                >
                  GitHub's privacy statement</a
                >. Search runs entirely in your browser via a static Pagefind index. Your theme
                choice is kept in your browser's local storage.
              </p>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-row">
              <h2>Comments and feedback</h2>
              <p>
                Blog comments and the support page's feedback box use Giscus, which stores
                comments as GitHub Discussions in a public repository. Commenting is optional and
                requires signing in with your GitHub account; anything you post is public and
                governed by GitHub's privacy statement and terms.
              </p>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-row">
              <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
              <p>
                If a future version changes what the app does with data, this page will be updated
                before that version is released, and the effective date revised.
              </p>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-row">
              <h2>Contact</h2>
              <p>
                Questions about this policy? Email
                <a href="mailto:studio@shravangoswami.com">studio@shravangoswami.com</a> or open
                an issue on GitHub.
              </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>

  <BackToTop />
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy-page {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
  }

  .legal-panel {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.95rem;
  }

  .privacy-strip {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.7rem;
  }

  .privacy-strip span {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.26rem 0.7rem;
    color: var(--text-soft);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    border: 1.8px solid var(--outline);
    background: var(--panel);
  }

  .privacy-strip strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 550;
  }

  .legal-copy {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
  }

  .legal-copy h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.26rem;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .legal-copy p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .legal-copy p + p {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
  }

  .policy-row {
    padding: 1.35rem 0 0;
  }
</style>
